==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From the surname of the two brothers who founded the company, Richard and Maurice McDonald.

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun|McDonald's|McDonald'ses}}

# A widespread chain of [[fast food]] [[restaurant]]s.
#* {{quote-book|en|title=An Evaluation of Fiscal Year 1968 Special Impact Programs|location=Bladensburg, Md.|publisher=Westinghouse Learning Corporation|year=1970|page=76|passage=This is evidence of the bank's confidence in a community organization for which it has now financed three ventures (CPI and two '''McDonald's''').}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=[[w:Time (magazine)|Time]]|year=1972|volume=101|page=31|column=1|passage=Today, blue-movie palaces are as much a part of the suburbs as the wildly proliferating '''McDonald’ses'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2019|author=[[w:Bernardine Evaristo|Bernardine Evaristo]]|title=[[w:Girl, Woman, Other|Girl, Woman, Other]] |publisher=Penguin Books (2020)|page=313|passage=she walked into a job in '''McDonaldʼs''', the first one she applied to}}

